    <h1 id="testing-markopress-with-custom-directories" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#testing-markopress-with-custom-directories">#</a> Testing MarkoPress with Custom Directories</h1>
<p>Today we’re testing MarkoPress with a custom content directory to demonstrate how flexible the configuration is.</p>
<h2 id="why-this-matters" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#why-this-matters">#</a> Why This Matters</h2>
<p>When building documentation sites or blogs, you often have existing content in a specific structure. MarkoPress lets you specify exactly where your content lives, rather than forcing you to reorganize everything.</p>
<h2 id="the-test-setup" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#the-test-setup">#</a> The Test Setup</h2>
<p>We created a test project with the following structure:</p>
<pre><code>test-project/
└── my-content/
    ├── pages/
    ├── docs/
    └── blog/
</code></pre>
<h2 id="configuration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#configuration">#</a> Configuration</h2>
<p>In <code>markopress.config.ts</code>:</p>
<pre class="shiki github-light" style="background-color:#fff;color:#24292e" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#D73A49">export</span><span style="color:#D73A49"> default</span><span style="color:#6F42C1"> defineConfig</span><span style="color:#24292E">({</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#24292E">  content: {</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#24292E">    pages: </span><span style="color:#032F62">'my-content/pages'</span><span style="color:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#24292E">    docs: </span><span style="color:#032F62">'my-content/docs'</span><span style="color:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#24292E">    blog: </span><span style="color:#032F62">'my-content/blog'</span><span style="color:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#24292E">  },</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="color:#24292E">});</span></span>
<span class="line"></span></code></pre>
<p>That’s it! MarkoPress now reads from <code>my-content/</code> instead of the default <code>content/</code> directory.</p>
<h2 id="what-works" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#what-works">#</a> What Works</h2>
<p>Everything works exactly the same:</p>
<ul>
<li>✅ Pages render at <code>/</code></li>
<li>✅ Docs with sidebar navigation</li>
<li>✅ Blog with RSS feeds</li>
<li>✅ Markdown processing</li>
<li>✅ Syntax highlighting</li>
<li>✅ Theme customization</li>
<li>✅ Plugin system</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="next-steps" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#next-steps">#</a> Next Steps</h2>
<p>Try it yourself:</p>
<ol>
<li>Create a new project</li>
<li>Configure custom content directories</li>
<li>Add your markdown files</li>
<li>Run <code>markopress dev</code></li>
</ol>
<p>Happy building!</p>

